Portions adapted from Blockyard (https://github.com/Potrock/blockyard), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Patrick Blais:
  src/server/lagcomp.ts (tick history with interpolated rewind, from src/platform/sim/hitscan.ts),
  src/shared/collision.ts (ray vs box slab test, from src/platform/sim/hitboxes.ts),
  src/server/room.ts and combat.ts (room step loop, spawn selection and kill/assist flow patterns from
  src/platform/host/room.ts and src/games/callofblocky/server.ts),
  src/client/netcode/interp.ts (snapshot playback against quickest delivery, from src/platform/client/interp.ts),
  src/client/netcode/predict.ts (predict/replay/ease-in reconciliation, from src/platform/client/predict.ts),
  src/shared/frontend/lobby.ts (map vote tally rule: most votes, ties to the earliest option, from src/games/callofblocky/nextvote.ts),
  src/server/features/modes/sd.ts and killcam.ts, src/client/features/modes/killcam.ts (Search and Destroy round
  flow and final-killcam timing patterns from src/games/callofblocky/briefcase.ts and killcam.ts),
  src/server/features/bots/nav.ts (walk/jump/drop cell grid and typed-array A* with a binary heap, from
  src/platform/kits/navgrid.ts), src/server/features/bots/brain.ts and aim.ts (react-then-settle aim,
  bursts, strafe timers, chasing heard/seen positions and unsticking, from src/platform/kits/shooterbot.ts
  and src/games/callofblocky/bots.ts),
  src/server/features/progression/tracker.ts (XP medal rules: first blood, multi-kill window, revenge, assists, and
  bots-never-earn, from src/games/callofblocky/progression.ts),
  src/server/features/killstreaks/streaks/mortar.ts (Mortar Team marks, staggered shells landing on the first
  surface under the spot, from src/games/callofblocky/streaks/mortar.ts), and the perk/streak rule shapes in
  src/server/features/perks and src/server/features/killstreaks (from src/games/callofblocky/perks.ts and streaks/).
Textures in assets/textures from Poly Haven (https://polyhaven.com), CC0.
Sound effects in assets/sfx cut from CC0 recordings: the Free Firearm Sound Library (Still North Media), Freesound,
  Kenney (Impact Sounds, Interface Sounds) and OpenGameArt contributors; per-file provenance in docs/audio/sfx-manifest.md.
